.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt HCLI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hcli
.Nd Hetzner Robot account and server-auction client
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Ar personality
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm market
.Op Fl C Ar bench
.Op Fl D Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl M Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl O Ar order
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm market_search
.Op Fl C Ar bench
.Op Fl D Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl M Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl O Ar order
.Op Fl X Ar text
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm market_show
.Fl i Ar product-id
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm market_order
.Fl i Ar product-id
.Op Fl k Ar fingerprint
.Op Fl T
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm traffic
.Op Fl f Ar from
.Op Fl t Ar to
.Op Fl i Ar server-number
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm rdns_set
.Fl i Ar address
.Fl n Ar ptr
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm vswitch_copy
.Fl r Ar reference
.Fl i Ar target
.Nm hcli
.Fl p Cm bring_online
.Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl g Ar pci
.Op Fl w Ar nic
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
talks to the Hetzner Robot web service.
The usual invocation is
.Pa ~/bin/hcli ,
which adds the
.Pa p5-WWW-req
and
.Pa p5-WWW-Hetzner
library trees and then runs this program.
.Pp
.Fl p
selects the personality.
An unknown name prints the list and exits 1.
Reads print and exit.
A write asks in
.Xr xmessage 1
first.
The default button is
.Cm no .
There is no timer.
If
.Ev DISPLAY
is empty it is set to
.Cm :0 .
Enter selects the default button.
.Cm z
prints
.Dq other: explain in the chat
and exits 0.
A failed
.Xr xmessage 1
is treated as no.
.Pp
The auction list is not printed while the download arrives.
.Fl p Cm market
and
.Fl p Cm market_search
read
.Pa ~/.cache/hetznercli/market.json
when it is still fresh, otherwise download the whole
product list and store it there.
The file lasts until the sooner of 30 minutes and the
soonest
.Va next_reduce
timer reaching zero.
Rows that miss a set floor are then dropped, and the
table is printed.
The default format measures each column from the rows
that remain.
The next run measures again.
In that table, text columns start under the header.
Number columns end on the header.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "EUR/TB" -compact
.It DC
Datacenter, with
.Ql -DC
shortened to
.Ql - .
.It prodid
Auction product id.
.It sys
Product name.
.It bench
CPU benchmark.
.It disk
Disk count times disk size, in gigabytes.
.It MEM
RAM in gigabytes.
.It EUR
Monthly price, two digits after the decimal.
.It EUR/TB
Monthly price per tebibyte, five digits after the decimal.
A tebibyte is the disk gigabytes divided by 1024.
A row with no disk prints
.Ql - .
.It next
Local
.Ql mmdd HH:MM
when the price next drops.
.It TB
Traffic, with a trailing
.Ql " TB"
removed.
.It CPU info
CPU description, unpadded.
.El
.Pp
.Fl o Cm format=price
prints fixed columns instead of the table above:
server id, RAM, total disk gigabytes, disk count, the
monthly price, euros per decimal terabyte to three places,
and the time left until the next drop.
That rate divides disk gigabytes by 1000.
The wide table divides by 1024 and keeps five decimal places.
The fixed columns can overflow.
The wide columns grow to each download.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "Fl k Ar fingerprint"
.It Fl c Ar file
ReadConf file.
The default is
.Pa ~/.hcli.conf .
The keys are
.Va huser
and
.Va hpass .
.It Fl C Ar bench
CPU benchmark floor for
.Cm market
and
.Cm market_search .
.Cm market_search
defaults to 5682.
.Cm market
applies it only when the flag is set.
.It Fl D Ar gigabytes
Disk floor, count times size, for
.Cm market
and
.Cm market_search .
.Cm market_search
defaults to 4096.
.Cm market
applies it only when the flag is set.
.Pp
A higher value raises
.Cm disk.min .
.It Fl f Ar from
First month of a
.Cm traffic
window.
Use with
.Fl t .
.Cm YYYY-MM
or
.Cm YYYY-MM-DD .
A day is reduced to its month.
.It Fl g Ar pci
PCI path for the
.Cm bring_online
NIC pin.
.Ql 0000:bb:dd.f
or the same string with a
.Ql pci-
prefix.
.It Fl i Ar id
Meaning depends on the personality:
server number for
.Cm traffic ,
auction product id for
.Cm market_show
and
.Cm market_order ,
address for
.Cm rdns_set ,
and target server number for
.Cm vswitch_copy .
.It Fl k Ar fingerprint
Stored Robot SSH key for
.Cm market_order .
Skips the key picker.
The confirm dialog still runs.
.It Fl M Ar gigabytes
RAM floor, in gigabytes, for
.Cm market
and
.Cm market_search .
.Cm market_search
defaults to 48.
.Cm market
applies it only when the flag is set.
.Pp
A higher value raises
.Cm mem.min .
.It Fl n Ar name
PTR name for
.Cm rdns_set ,
or the short host name for
.Cm bring_online .
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Repeatable auction option.
One
.Fl o
may list several
.Cm key=value
pairs separated by commas.
.Pp
.Fl o Cm re=ECC,re=ENT
is two required patterns.
A comma that is not followed by
.Cm key=
stays in the value.
Only
.Cm market
and
.Cm market_search
accept it.
Anywhere else it prints
.Ql -o is only for market and market_search
and exits 1.
A bare
.Fl o
prints
.Ql -o needs key=value
and exits 1.
.Bl -tag -width "disk.count=min:max" -compact
.It Cm format=full
The wide table above.
This is the default.
.Cm market
appends
.Ql auction servers: N .
.Cm market_search
omits that line.
.It Cm format=price
Fixed columns: id, RAM, disk gigabytes, disk count,
monthly price, euros per decimal terabyte to three places,
and the time until the next drop.
A future drop prints days and
.Ql HH:MM:SS ,
then
.Ql aka
and the local
.Ql YYYYMMDD HH:MM:SS .
A non-positive
.Va next_reduce
prints
.Cm fixed
when
.Va fixed_price
is true, otherwise
.Cm reload .
This format omits the server count.
.It Cm format=custom:...
Recognized and refused with
.Ql format=custom is not implemented .
.It Cm disk.min Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm disk.max Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm disk Ns = Ns Ar min:max
Total disk gigabytes, count times size, inclusive.
A later minimum only rises.
A later maximum only falls.
.It Cm disk.count.min Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm disk.count.max Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm disk.count Ns = Ns Ar min:max
Disk count, inclusive.
The same later-bound rule applies.
.It Cm mem.min Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm mem.max Ns = Ns Ar n
.It Cm mem Ns = Ns Ar min:max
RAM gigabytes, inclusive.
The same later-bound rule applies.
.It Cm price.min Ns = Ns Ar eur
.It Cm price.max Ns = Ns Ar eur
.It Cm price Ns = Ns Ar min:max
Monthly price in euros, inclusive.
.It Cm re Ns = Ns Ar pattern
A Perl regular expression.
Every
.Cm re
must match.
A later
.Fl o Cm re
adds another required pattern.
.Pp
.Xr hmktvm 1
passes
.Cm ECC
and
.Cm ENT
this way so a row needs both tags.
A bar inside one pattern is or.
The searched text is the disk line, the CPU line, and the
description.
.It Cm sort Ns = Ns Ar field
Sort the printed rows.
A later
.Cm sort
replaces an earlier one.
A leading minus reverses the order.
The numeric fields are
.Cm price ,
.Cm mem ,
.Cm eur/tb ,
.Cm disk ,
.Cm disk.count ,
.Cm bench ,
.Cm id ,
and
.Cm next .
.Cm eur/tb
is monthly euros per tebibyte of disk.
Aliases include
.Cm cost_per_tb
and
.Cm price_per_tb .
A row with no disk sorts last on
.Cm eur/tb .
The text fields are
.Cm dc ,
.Cm cpu ,
and
.Cm name .
.El
An unknown key prints
.Ql unknown option
and the key.
An unknown format prints
.Ql unknown format
and the value.
A bad number prints the key and
.Ql needs a number .
A bad range prints the key and
.Ql needs MIN:MAX .
An empty pattern prints
.Ql re needs a pattern .
A pattern that does not compile prints
.Ql bad re .
A minimum above its maximum is an error.
.Fl D
raises the disk minimum when
.Fl D
is higher.
A smaller
.Cm disk.min
does not lower
.Fl D .
.Pp
.Fl M
raises
.Cm mem.min
the same way.
.It Fl O Ar order
Deprecated alias for
.Fl o Cm sort= Ns Ar order
when no
.Fl o Cm sort
is set.
.Cm mem
and
.Cm price
are the old names.
.Fl o Cm sort
wins when both are given.
.It Fl p Ar personality
Which Robot call to make.
Required.
.It Fl r Ar server
Reference server number for
.Cm vswitch_copy .
.It Fl t Ar to
Last month of a
.Cm traffic
window.
Use with
.Fl f .
Same date forms as
.Fl f .
.It Fl T
Add
.Ql test=true
to a
.Cm market_order
post.
Robot accepts it and does not provision the server.
The confirm dialog still runs.
.It Fl v
Accepted and ignored.
.It Fl w Ar nic
Interface name for the
.Cm bring_online
NIC pin, such as
.Ql eno2 .
.It Fl X Ar text
Accepted on
.Cm market_search .
The default is
.Cm Ent .
It is not sent on the download, and it is not applied to CPU or disk text.
.El
.Sh PERSONALITIES
.Bl -tag -width "market_transactions"
.It Cm ip
Dump the account IP list.
.It Cm servers
One block per server: number, name, paid-until date, the
.Ql ::2
address from
.Va server_ipv6_net ,
the gateway from the subnet list, an IPv4 address when
.Va server_ip
is a dotted quad, and the PTR of that
.Ql ::2
address.
.It Cm reset
List server number, server IP, and the reset types Robot offers.
This does not reboot a server.
A server with no IPv4 can make the IP column warn.
.It Cm subnet
Dump the subnet list.
.It Cm rdns
Dump every reverse-DNS record on the account.
.It Cm rdns_set
Print the current PTR of
.Fl i ,
then ask before posting
.Fl n .
The default button is
.Cm no .
.It Cm sshkey
Dump the SSH keys stored in Robot.
.It Cm products
Dump the full-price dedicated catalog,
.Ql GET /order/server/product .
This is not the server auction.
.It Cm storagebox
Dump the storage-box list.
.It Cm server_transactions
Dump dedicated-server orders.
An empty list prints
.Dq no server transactions
and exits 0.
A missing document exits 2.
.It Cm market_transactions
Dump auction orders.
An empty list prints
.Dq no market transactions
and exits 0.
A missing document exits 2.
.It Cm traffic
Monthly totals for the last six calendar months,
including the current month, unless
.Fl f
and
.Fl t
both set another window.
One end alone is an error.
The post uses each server's IPv6 prefix and any real IPv4 address.
.Fl i
keeps one server number.
Gigabytes in, out, and sum are printed per address.
A prefix with no samples prints
.Dq no samples .
A month that has not closed can come back as zero.
.It Cm market
Download every current auction server.
Robot ignores query filters on this call, so none are sent.
Rows must pass any
.Fl C ,
.Fl D ,
.Fl M ,
or
.Fl o
bound that was set.
There is no default floor.
The default print is the wide table.
Its last line is
.Ql auction servers: N .
.Fl o Cm format=price
prints the fixed price table and omits that line.
.It Cm market_search
Same download as
.Cm market .
Rows under the
.Fl C ,
.Fl D ,
and
.Fl M
floors are dropped.
Those floors default to 5682, 4096, and 48.
.Fl o
bounds apply as well.
The count line is omitted.
.Fl X
is accepted and is not matched against CPU or disk text.
.It Cm market_show
Print one auction server: id, name, datacenter, CPU and
benchmark, RAM, disks, description, monthly, hourly, and
setup price, price per tebibyte to two decimals, traffic,
the next drop, and the network speed.
Requires
.Fl i .
.It Cm market_order
Print the same stats as
.Cm market_show ,
then ask which stored Robot key to install.
An ED25519 key is the recommended default.
.Fl k
selects a key without that dialog.
A second dialog, default
.Cm no ,
shows the post body.
The post is IPv6-only:
.Va product_id
and
.Va authorized_key[] ,
plus
.Va test
when
.Fl T
is set.
No password, no comment, and no
.Va primary_ipv4
addon.
A comment would make Robot process the order by hand.
Ordering must be enabled on the account.
The account allows about 20 order calls a day.
The reply's server number stays empty until the machine is provisioned.
.It Cm vswitch_copy
Print the vSwitches present on
.Fl r
and absent from
.Fl i .
A list row with no server array is fetched again.
Unknown membership is an error, not an empty attachment list.
The default button is
.Cm no .
On yes, each missing vSwitch is attached.
.Ql VSWITCH_IN_PROCESS
is retried three times, five seconds apart.
A later read must show the target on each posted vSwitch.
.It Cm bring_online
Print the SSH
.Va HostKeyAlias
block, the NIC pin, the todd user step, and the port 8006 certificate step for
.Fl n Ns \&.fdh.bz .
The name is lowercased and a trailing
.Ql .fdh.bz
is removed.
.Cm pxj
prints the plan and does not ask, ssh, or append.
Any other name asks before each of the four steps.
The default button is
.Cm no .
The SSH block sets aliases only.
It does not copy local forwards.
The NIC files are printed when both
.Fl g
and
.Fl w
are set.
Saying yes prints them again and does not copy them.
They have to be on the rescue image before the first disk boot.
The todd step reads
.Ev HETZNER_USER_CONF
or
.Pa ~/.config/hetzner/todd.conf ,
refuses to print the hash, and runs
.Ql ssh r. Ns Ar name .
The certificate step is the Proxmox ACME order for that host name.
The contact is
.Mt postmaster@fdh.bz .
A certificate that is already issued is left in place.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa ~/.hcli.conf
Robot user and password.
Mode 600.
.It Pa ~/bin/hcli
Wrapper that supplies the Perl library path.
.It Pa ~/.config/hetzner/todd.conf
Hash file for
.Cm bring_online .
One ReadConf line,
.Va hash ,
holding a
.Ql $2a$ ,
.Ql $2b$ ,
or
.Ql $2y$
hash.
The hash is not printed.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
Appended only after a yes on
.Cm bring_online .
.It Pa ~/.cache/hetznercli/market.json
Cached auction list.
Mode 600.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std hcli
A Robot 404 or
.Ql NOT_FOUND
document prints one line and exits 2.
Other Robot errors print
.Ql api
and the status, code, and message, and exit 1.
Declining a write, or choosing
.Cm z ,
exits 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Auction table, columns fitted to this download:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p market
.Pp
Same list in the fixed price table, with both tags required:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p market -o format=price,re=ECC,re=ENT
.Pp
Cheapest tebibyte first:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p market -o sort=eur/tb
.Pp
One auction server:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p market_show -i 2799696
.Pp
Six months of traffic for every server:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p traffic
.Pp
Plan for a new host, without running the steps:
.Pp
.Dl ~/bin/hcli -p bring_online -n pxk
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hinstall 1 ,
.Xr hmktst 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm-picky 1 ,
.Xr xmessage 1
